      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I completely understand your frustration, and it's important to weigh the risks when you're experiencing discomfort. While a single dose of Sudafed might not be significantly dangerous, it can raise your blood pressure dramatically in some people. Over time, regular use could pose more serious health risks, especially as you're on antipsychotics which already affect your cardiovascular system. It's best to check with your pharmacist about the risks, and better yet, have a conversation with your doctor about your side effects and the safest alternatives. Your health and peace of mind are vital.",
